## 1. M6-SEC-1: one low in a graduation's warm-up second

ECON §10.1's graduation rows (migration 2 s after the completion, the keeper cranking every second): in the
k-th second after the transition (k = 1: the first post-change bucket) the attacker sends [sell to f x the
pool's spot, crank_price, buy back] next to the keeper's crank, so that bucket's low is f x the price.  As built
the warm-up seed is the lowest post-change bucket low (bounded upward only), so one such low sets P_ema for the
rest of the warm-up and the EMA leg then climbs back at most one v0.4.1 step (x7/6) a second; with M6-SEC-1
the seed also falls by at most one step (x11/12) per integration.  Cells: the exit (seconds after the
completion, price), lenders' tokens back + SOL; the attacker's round trip (SOL, fees at the pool's tier).

