## 3. M6R-1 in steady state on a PumpSwap pool (market C: the fresh graduate after its boost, Tier C)

(a) A deposit of k x the pool held for H and pulled in the second a genuine 3x/120 s pump starts (the keeper on
its coverage duties, #101 keeper).  L_ema and L_slow follow the deeper pool while it is held; the exit reference
L_b = max(L_live, min(max(L_ema', L_slow), cap)) then credits the pulled depth unless the cap floor(D*1e4/
lambda_min) binds -- under #106 lambda_min = 100 % on PumpSwap, so the cap is D and L_b the drained pool's own
depth.  Cells: the exit (seconds after the pump starts, price); L_b / the pool's depth at the pump's first
second.

