(f) The reference cap under #106.  #106 credits a canonical PumpSwap pool with its burned depth D alone: it
sizes positions on D and (M6E-1) caps the exit reference's EMA terms at D, so L_b = max(L_live, min(max(L_ema',
L_slow), D)) is L_live itself (D <= L_live on a canonical pool).  Ref2D is #106 as first written: sizing on D,
the reference cap kept at floor(D*1e4/pool_lock_min_bps) = 2D, so the EMA terms (V2-14: quiet-second
withdrawals cannot lower the reference) could still credit a pulled deposit up to twice the drained depth.

