(iv) M6E-1: an expiry after a deposit pulled at the deadline.  A position of `size` x the cap (sized on D) held
to its deadline (Tier C, 7 d; the keeper cranking every 600 s); an LP deposits k x the pool an hour before the
deadline and holds it (a crank every 30 s: L_slow, tau 1 h, follows the deeper pool), withdrawing every
third-party unit at the deadline (or 600 / 1,800 s before); from the deadline the keeper cranks and tries
expire every second.  The expiry bound is B_ref*(1 + delta_exp), delta_exp = 1 %: a buyback on the drained
pool costs (1 - c/2)/(1 - c) - 1 more than a reference at twice its depth, 1.2 % at c = q/X = 2.35 %, so a
reference that still credits the pulled deposit refuses it until L_slow has decayed.  Cells: the expiry,
seconds after the deadline; L_b / the pool's depth at the first try:

